# Snyk policy for the repo root (`snyk code test`). Snyk Code supports only path excludes
# here (per-finding ignores live in the Snyk UI), so keep each entry to one exact file and
# say why. platform/.snyk holds the dependency ignores for platform/.
version: v1.25.0
exclude:
  code:
    # Insecure-XML-parser warning only applies to Python < 3.11; we run >=3.11. Test fixtures.
    - tests/unit/visualizer/test_namespaces.py
    # Dev tooling, not shipped: --root comes from the developer's own command line
    # (same class as the other wiki-librarian tool findings ignored as "By design").
    - .claude/skills/wiki-librarian/tools/build_status.py
    # LLM_PROVIDER_CONFIG_PATH is an operator-set config location by design, not user input.
    - platform/packages/llm-provider-config/src/llm_provider_config/store.py
    # 2 HIGH "XSS" findings (be99614e-.../line 428, 4bf0d945-.../line 473): Snyk Code's
    # taint engine flags object_id/description/view_id -> Response(content=svg) without
    # recognizing rendering.sanitize_svg() (defused-XML, strips script/foreignObject/
    # iframe/on*/javascript:/data:) as a sanitizer. The request params are only ever used
    # as a whitelist lookup key into views.yaml, never as content. sanitize_svg() is now
    # called a second time at this file's two response sinks as well, so the dataflow is
    # sanitized both upstream and at the sink. CSP `sandbox` + `nosniff` headers on every
    # response are a further backstop. Formal per-finding ignore via `snyk ignore create`
    # was attempted and blocked (org lacks "Consistent Ignores for Snyk Code"); this path
    # exclude is the fallback until that's enabled or a Web UI ignore is recorded.
    - platform/packages/modelling-specification/src/modelling_specification/router.py
